han $40 million, while Collins has raised under $8 million. Outside spending has been modest on both sides.\n\nEvery recent poll, including surveys from Republican-leaning pollsters like Trafalgar, Rasmussen, and InsiderAdvantage, shows Ossoff ahead, with most margins between four and eleven points. Prediction markets price his win probability at 93 to 95 percent, and most expert raters place the race in the Likely D column. The NRSC has not listed Georgia among its top targets, though Thune has campaigned for Collins. The race appears settled in Ossoff's favor barring a major late shift.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9499, "margin": 8.78}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9449, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9229, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9348, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9317, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9355, "margin": 8.5}]}